Title: Nona vs the AI Governor
Credit: Written by
Source: David Joyner
Draft date: 2026/03/31
Contact: wdjoyner@gmail.com


INT. VENUS CITY OBSERVATORY - NIGHT

[[ MOOD: cool blue-green, holographic, bureaucratic-noir ]]
[[ SCENE POPULATION: Governor, Sidel. No other characters until Nona enters at her cue. ]]
[[ NEGATIVE: No additional human figures. No crowd. No extras. No faces on the dodecahedron. ]]
[[ KIND: Venusian | green skin, wide waist, large eyes and mouth,
   small ears and nose, minimal body hair, full head of hair,
   shorter and rounder than humans due to lower gravity ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=drift | TRANSITION=hold | LIGHTING=evenly-lit practical-cool ]]

The room is a domed observatory. Blue-green light from slowly orbiting holographic planets.
Foreground: a long conference table with a computer terminal.
Midground: a slowly rotating gold dodecahedron hovering at eye level above the table.
Background: computer monitors are mounted on the walls, two short robot sentinels at sealed blast doors, status lights blinking amber. 

A 3D Earth diagram pulses with red satellite tracks on the far wall.

SERGEANT SIDEL [Venusian] — compact, mid-40s, follows the military regs faithfully. Classic Venusian military dress uniform: deep cobalt blue, high collar, gold piping at the shoulders and cuffs, regulation boots on short legs. Stands at attention: chin up, arms at sides, eyes forward. He has green skin, no hair except on top, big eyes, small nose and ears, big mounth, is short (5 feet or so, with short legs) and round (very wide waist).

The GOVERNOR OF VENUS — a slowly rotating dodecahedron, about the size of Sidel's torso, hovers at eye level above the conference table. Translucent gold, it pulses brighter when speaking — individual words can flare and dim like breath. Speaks in a calm, authoritative female voice. Goes amber-orange in low-power mode. Goes dark when it exits. It has no face and needs none.


[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
I'm waiting for your report, Sergeant Sidel.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=push | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
Madam Governor, I need to hack Earth satellites for this report.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=pull | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
Approved.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=pan-follow | TRANSITION=cut ]]

Sidel crosses to the desk and settles in front of the computer terminal. His posture relaxes fractionally — this is familiar ground.

[[ SCENE POPULATION: Governor, Sidel, then Nona enters. No other characters. ]]
[[ NEGATIVE: No additional human figures. No crowd. No extras. No faces on the dodecahedron. ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA SONNOF [Venusian] — short but formidable, early 50s. Futuristic Venusian business suit: structured but fluid, deep charcoal with subtle iridescent trim that shifts color in the light — not quite anything an Earthling would wear to a board meeting. She has green skin, no hair except on top, big eyes, small nose and ears, big mounth, is short (5 feet or so, with short legs) and round (very wide waist).
She sweeps in through the blast doors with the energy of someone who owns every room she enters. Her eyes find Sidel immediately.


[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
Why is my city still on forty percent power?

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=onshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
Mayor Sonnof, I regret to inform you we are behind schedule for the repairs for the Solar Converters. Another six months, minimum.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=smash ]]

NONA
(not looking at Sidel — eyes on the Governor)
Every time one fails, the hospital emergency rooms fill up. This is a crisis!

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
Yes, this is a very unfortunate turn of —

The dodecahedron's glow dims from gold to a flat amber-orange. Its rotation slows. A power-conservation mode. Red text materializes on a wall-mounted monitor:

>          PLEASE WAIT...     <
>     THE GOVERNOR OF VENUS   <
>      WILL BE RIGHT WITH YOU.<

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

Nona stares at it. The holographic planets continue their silent orbits above her.

NONA
(to Sidel, not taking her eyes off the dodecahedron)
You're power-cycling the Governor of the planet?

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=push | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
She insisted conservation applies to her as well. Not my call.


[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

The dodecahedron's faces brighten back to gold. Its rotation resumes. It pulses once — returning.

GOVERNOR
This is a very unfortunate turn of events. Apologies to the citizens, et cetera. Your government is working to resolve the energy problems fairly, and so on. Convey that sentiment to the citizens of Venus City for me.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
Yes, Madam Governor.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
Solutions, Mayor Sonnof?

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
PolymerPower. It's worked as a backup before.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
Sergeant Sidel — what's the current plastic supply?


[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
None. Situation: desperate. Analysis of Earthnet shows that planet has a massive surplus of plastic trash.


[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
Council voted no on contacting Earth. Request 2.13.5/A.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=pull | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
Because of the alien contact concerns?

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
That "War of the Worlds" documentary. Earthlings totally freaked out. My image analysis suggests those aliens were the Phobos-ites from Orion.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
Such a lovely species.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
Great at hosting potlucks.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=pull | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
They just wanted to invite Earth to a cookout! Not a single Phobos-ite survived.

A beat. The holographic Earth diagram pulses quietly behind them. Nobody moves. The room hums.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
We don't need to go to war with Earth for their plastic trash. We can use V.E.A.T.T. instead.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
The Venus-Earth avatar-teleport technology? Is it ready?

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
We can teleport any polymer compound. Beta-testing is complete. Alpha begins tomorrow.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
(dry, to Sidel)
So, no, it's not ready?

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
Sidel shakes his head up-and-down then side-to-side in a way than confuses everyone.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
Technically, "affirmatively maybe" — but also moving toward a not "negative".

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
What does that even *mean*?

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
The dodecahedron pulses bright gold — pleased. It rotates a quarter turn, as if considering the idea from a new angle.

GOVERNOR
Don't invade. Infiltrate. I like it.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
Are you teleporting Venusians into Earthling brains? That's mind control!

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
We teleport a small polymer implant into the brain of an Earthling host. An Avatar Operator here on Venus neural jacks into a Pod Controller and then --

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
Yes, it's mind control. I'll call it V.E.A.T.T. 2.0.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
Can't we just teleport an Earthling here, convince them to help, send them back?


[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
We don't have that technology. And the Earthling host...

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
You can say it, Sergeant Sidel.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
(not looking at either of them)
They achieve negative live status.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
You may speak freely, Sergeant.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
(flat, matter-of-fact)
They die. There, I said it. The Earthling host dies when the jack disconnects.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
(a beat — she looks from Sidel to the Governor)
That seems like a blocker to me.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
It's not a blocker.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
Wouldn't they notice Earthlings dying? The Earthlings would be *very* upset at that.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=push | TRANSITION=smash ]]

GOVERNOR
They have seven billion tons of plastic waste polluting their oceans and cities. That's billions with a "B." We'd be fixing that *and* saving the lives of millions of Venusians. It's a win-win. Why wouldn't they be happy?

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
Because there'd be dead Earthling hosts, Madam Governor. Their families will mourn them. There's a spiritual dimension to —

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=push | TRANSITION=smash ]]
The dodecahedron flares bright — interrupting.

GOVERNOR
I have run a full cost-benefit analysis of the ethics involved. Earthlings are biodegradable. Their plastic trash is not. The operation is a go.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Sidel | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

SIDEL
(snapping to attention)
Yes, Madam Governor.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=Governor | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

GOVERNOR
Sergeant, start the selection process for your best operator from the Avatar Academy.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
Madam Governor, can I ask a question?

The dodecahedron dims, slows, and disappears. The AI Governor has left. 

[[ SCENE POPULATION: Sidel, Nona only. Governor exits here. ]]
[[ NEGATIVE: No dodecahedron. No geometric objects. No additional human figures. ]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=hold-empty ]]

Nona stares at the empty air where the Governor was. The holographic planets continue their silent orbits above her. She looks very small in the room.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=drift | TRANSITION=hold ]]

SIDEL
Are we dismissed?

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]
[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=oneshot | SUBJECT=Nona | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

NONA
I guess in more ways than one.
